---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Design cookbook · Pace"
  description="Design recipes for the Pace marketplace. "
  activeNav="cookbook"
  canonicalPath="/cookbook/design"
>
  <article class="usecases-page">
    <header class="usecases-team-page-head">
      <a class="usecases-back-link" href="/cookbook">&larr; All cookbooks</a>
      <span class="usecases-eyebrow">Design cookbook</span>
      <h1>Design</h1>
      <p class="usecases-team-page-tagline">Design audits on every PR. Brand-voice enforcement on shipped content. Defers to impeccable for the frontend craft Pace doesn't own.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="usecases-team-page-body">
        <article class="usecase-card usecase-card-marquee">
          <span class="usecase-card-badge">Marquee recipe</span>
          <h3>Per-PR design audit before review</h3>
          <p class="usecase-outcome">Design regressions caught before a reviewer ever clicks "request changes".</p>
          <p>Every PR touching CSS / JSX / Vue templates runs <code>/impeccable audit</code> against the changed files. Findings (contrast issues, anti-pattern hits from impeccable's 50+ detection rules, layout regressions) post as inline comments. Reviewers see the design diff alongside the code diff.</p>
          <dl class="usecase-meta">
            <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, GitHub trigger on <code>pull_request.opened</code> against frontend repos</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>/impeccable audit</code>, <code>/impeccable critique</code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (GitHub trigger), inline PR comments, plan mode for fixes</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <aside class="design-defers">
          <div class="design-defers-text">
            <span class="design-defers-eyebrow">Why design defers</span>
            <h3>Pace defers to impeccable for frontend craft.</h3>
            <p>
              <a href="https://impeccable.style">Impeccable</a> is a separate Apache 2.0 skill kit focused entirely on frontend craft for AI coding agents. One router (<code>/impeccable</code>) with 23 sub-commands across typography, color, layout, motion, accessibility, UX writing, design systems, and dev handoff. It runs in every harness Pace runs in (Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI, and 8 more).
            </p>
            <p>
              Pace's site, build pipeline, and multi-harness install machinery were forked from impeccable; the two projects share a maintainer ethos but ship independently.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="design-defers-cta">
            <a href="https://impeccable.style" class="cta cta-primary">Visit impeccable.style</a>
            <a href="https://impeccable.style/docs" class="cta cta-secondary">Read the impeccable docs</a>
          </div>
        </aside>

<div class="usecases-impeccable">
        <div class="usecases-impeccable-grid">
          <article class="usecase-card">
            <h3>Brand-voice enforcement on every PR</h3>
            <p class="usecase-outcome">Voice drift caught before it ships, not after the campaign runs.</p>
            <p>Any PR that touches landing pages, blog posts, or email templates auto-runs <code>brand-voice-enforcement</code> from the brand-voice plugin and posts inline comments with concrete fixes. Pairs with the marketing plugin's <code>draft-content</code> when a section needs a rewrite from scratch.</p>
            <dl class="usecase-meta">
              <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, GitHub trigger on <code>pull_request.opened</code> for content/CMS repos</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>brand-voice-enforcement</code>, <code>draft-content</code></dd></div>
              <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (GitHub trigger), inline PR comments, plan mode</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </article>

          <article class="usecase-card">
            <h3>Polish pass on a feature branch</h3>
            <dl class="usecase-meta">
              <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Interactive, before merging a feature</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>/impeccable polish</code>, <code>/impeccable typeset</code>, <code>/impeccable layout</code></dd></div>
              <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Multi-skill chain, plan mode</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p>Before merging, run <code>/impeccable polish</code> on the branch. The router orchestrates typography, color, layout, and motion sub-commands; plan mode shows the diff before anything ships. The polish pass is what turns a working feature into one that feels intentional.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="usecase-card">
            <h3>Cross-tool design system sync</h3>
            <dl class="usecase-meta">
              <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Interactive, when tokens or components change</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>design-system</code> (Pace), <code>/impeccable colorize</code> + <code>/impeccable typeset</code> (impeccable)</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Cross-plugin chain, MCP connector to Figma</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p>Pace's <code>/design</code> plugin manages the system at the spec level (Figma tokens, contribution model, dev handoff). Impeccable's <code>/colorize</code> and <code>/typeset</code> apply those tokens in code with full understanding of how they look on screen. Use both: the design plugin sets the rules, impeccable enforces them in the codebase.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="usecases-impeccable-cta">
          <a href="https://impeccable.style" class="cta cta-primary">Visit impeccable.style</a>
          <a href="https://impeccable.style/docs" class="cta cta-secondary">Read the impeccable docs</a>
        </div>

        <details class="usecases-impeccable-when">
          <summary>When to use Pace's <code>/design</code> plugin vs impeccable</summary>
          <p>Different layers of the same craft:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Pace <code>/design</code></strong> covers UX research, design system management, accessibility audits at the policy level, dev handoff, and research synthesis. Use it for the work a design <em>team</em> does.</li>
            <li><strong>Impeccable</strong> covers the visual + interaction craft of writing the UI code itself: typography choices, color tokens, spatial rhythm, motion design, responsive layout. Use it for the work a designer would obsess over when looking at the rendered pixels.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Most teams want both. Install impeccable alongside Pace; the Pace CLI (<code>npx pace skills install</code>) offers it during setup.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Accessibility audit before every release</h3>
        <p>Before merging the release branch, a routine runs an accessibility sweep across the changed pages: WCAG 2.1 AA checks, keyboard-navigation flow, color contrast against the design tokens, screen-reader labeling. Findings post as a single triaged issue per release: P0 must-fix, P1 should-fix, P2 worth-noting.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, GitHub trigger on release-branch creation</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>accessibility-audit</code>, <code>/impeccable audit</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (GitHub trigger), GitHub Issues integration, axe-core via MCP</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </article>
    </div>

    <footer class="usecases-footer">
      <p>
        Have a design workflow that should live here? <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/issues/new">Open an issue</a> with the trigger, skills, and Claude features it uses; we'll fold it into the cookbook.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .usecases-page {
    max-width: var(--width-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-3xl);
  }
  .usecases-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .usecases-lede strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* Engineering callout above the TOC */
  .usecases-eng-callout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.78;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out-quart);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecases-eng-callout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: var(--spacing-md);
    }
  }

  /* TOC grid */
  .usecases-toc {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  .usecases-toc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    display: block;
    margin: 0 6px var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .usecases-toc-name {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-toc-count {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-ash);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .usecases-toc-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .usecases-team {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .usecases-team-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-team-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-team-tagline {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecase-card-marquee {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-paper-elev) 92%, var(--color-forest-dim));
  }
  .usecase-card-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecase-card-badge::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecase-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .usecase-card > p {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
  }
  /* Meta: small chip row at the bottom (was a big dl block at top) */
  .usecase-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 8px;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta > div {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .usecase-meta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .usecase-meta dt::after {
    content: ":";
    margin-left: 1px;
    color: var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .usecase-meta dd code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }
  .usecase-card p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card p code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-footer {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .usecases-footer a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch a,
  .usecases-impeccable-when a,
  .usecases-team-tagline a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch code,
  .usecases-impeccable-when code,
  .usecases-team-tagline code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart), color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .cta-primary {
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }
  .cta-primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-hover);
  }
  .cta-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .cta-secondary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary::before {
    content: '+';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-right: var(--spacing-sm);
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when[open] summary::before {
    content: '−';
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when p,
  .usecases-impeccable-when ul {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecase-meta > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2px;
    }
  }

  /* Recipe card outcome-first ordering: prose before pills */
  .usecase-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .usecase-card h3 { order: 1; }
  .usecase-card-badge { order: 0; }
  .usecase-card > p { order: 2; }
  .usecase-card .usecase-meta { order: 3; margin-top: var(--spacing-md); }


  /* Outcome line at the top of every marquee card. Big bold one-liner
     that tells the visitor what they actually get before the prose. */
  .design-defers {
    margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0 var(--spacing-xl);
    padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-xl);
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--spacing-xl);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .design-defers-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .design-defers-eyebrow::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .design-defers-text h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .design-defers-text p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .design-defers-cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .design-defers {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: var(--spacing-md);
    }
  }

  .usecase-outcome {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-forest);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
  }
  .usecase-setup-title {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
